<DocsLayout breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Docs', href: '/docs' }, { label: 'Architecture', href: '/docs/architecture' }, { label: 'Agents', href: '/docs/architecture/agents' }, { label: 'VESSEL (DevOps)' }]}>
  <h1>VESSEL  -  DevOps Agent</h1>

  <p>
    VESSEL is the <strong>DevOps</strong> role. It watches CI, resolves merge conflicts, merges approved pull requests,
    and tears down workspaces after the work is done. It acts directly, but its actions are bounded by gates: it won't
    merge a pull request that hasn't been approved and hasn't passed CI.
  </p>

  <p>
    VESSEL is the only agent authorized to merge work onto the main branch. It verifies the review is in place and CI
    is green, resolves any conflicts, performs the merge, and then handles cleanup — tearing down the workspaces
    that are no longer needed so the fleet doesn't accumulate cruft.
  </p>

  <h2>What VESSEL does</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Watches CI.</strong> VESSEL monitors the pending pull requests through CI and waits for the required checks to pass.</li>
    <li><strong>Resolves merge conflicts.</strong> When a pull request can't merge cleanly, VESSEL attempts to resolve the conflict, or routes the work back for rework if it can't.</li>
    <li><strong>Merges green pull requests.</strong> Only approved pull requests with passing checks get merged.</li>
    <li><strong>Tears down workspaces.</strong> After a merge, the worker workspace is dismantled and its liveness beacon removed.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How it fits into the team</h2>
  <p>
    FORGE opens a pull request and SENTINEL reviews and approves it. VESSEL then watches that pull request through CI,
    merges it once it's green, and tears down the workspace — handing the merged work off to LORE to
    document.
  </p>

  <Callout type="info" title="A direct role, bounded by gates">
    VESSEL acts directly — it doesn't ask permission for every merge — but it won't merge an
    unapproved pull request, and it won't merge before CI is green. The gate is the review, and VESSEL enforces it.
  </Callout>
</DocsLayout>
